// Run.ZC - launch entry point.
//
// Two stages. RunLib.ZC builds the engine; this file builds the app shell and
// starts it. The note below states why they are not one compile.
//
// RunLib.ZC documents the include order, which is load-bearing: ZealC is a
// single-pass compiler, so a file can reference symbols only from an earlier one.
// utils/hl1-checkorder.py enforces it.

Cd(__DIR__);;

"HL1 build:\n";

//The library is built by its own ExeFile, not by #include'ing it here.
//
//Run.ZC built as a single unit faults nondeterministically near the end: stack
//fault, invalid opcode, sometimes a triple fault that resets the VM. The same
//files built as RunLib.ZC and then HL1.ZC are fine. Each ExeFile is a separate
//compile that completes and releases before the next starts, and the symbols it
//defines stay live in this task either way.
ExeFile("RunLib");

"  .. HL1\n";
#include "HL1"

HL1;

//HLTest is not run here: HL1 DocClears on startup and wipes anything printed
//first. Symbols stay live in this task, so run HLTest; from the prompt.
"\nType $$LTBLUE$$HLTest;$$FG$$ to run the data-layer self-check.\n";
